3. 養聲

廣東話：佢係歌手，所以平時好注重養聲。
English: He is a singer, so he usually pays a lot of attention to taking care of his voice.

4. 票尾

廣東話：你記得留返張飛嘅票尾，等陣要對數。
English: Remember to keep the ticket stub; you'll need it for reconciliation later.

5. hacker

廣東話：個 hacker 入侵咗公司嘅伺服器，偷咗好多客戶資料。
English: The hacker broke into the company's server and stole a lot of customer data.

6. 石斛蘭

廣東話：呢盆石斛蘭依附喺樹幹上面生長，開出嚟嘅花好靚。
English: This dendrobium orchid grows attached to the tree trunk, and its flowers are very beautiful.

7. 吊詭

廣東話：呢個情況好吊詭，明明證據都喺度，但係佢就死口唔認。
English: This situation is very paradoxical; the evidence is right there, but he stubbornly refuses to admit it.

8. 吊詭

廣東話：佢話自己好忙，但係又成日見到佢喺度發呆，真係吊詭。
English: He says he's very busy, but he's always seen spacing out; it's really absurd.

9. 各為其主

廣東話：兩隊人馬喺商場入面對峙，其實都係各為其主，冇必要鬧到咁僵。
English: The two teams are confronting each other in the mall; they're just each serving their own masters, so there's no need to make things so awkward.

10. 軨蓋

廣東話：你部車嘅軨蓋爛咗，快啲換咗佢啦。
English: The hubcap on your car is broken; you should replace it soon.

11. 打哥夫

廣東話：佢退休之後，日日都去球場打哥夫。
English: After he retired, he goes to the golf course every day to play golf.

12. 免揀

廣東話：呢批貨係免揀嘅，你鍾意唔鍾意都要收貨。
English: This batch of goods is non-selectable; you have to accept it whether you like it or not.

13. 擺闊佬

廣東話：佢成日喺朋友面前擺闊佬，其實背後負債累累。
English: He always shows off his wealth in front of friends, but he's actually deeply in debt behind the scenes.

14. 廣播劇

廣東話：我細個嗰陣好鍾意聽收音機嘅廣播劇。
English: When I was young, I loved listening to radio dramas on the radio.

15. 錄影機

廣東話：以前屋企部錄影機壞咗，我哋就冇得睇錄影帶。
English: When the VCR at home broke down, we couldn't watch videotapes anymore.

16. 吟詩吟唔甩

廣東話：證據咁清楚，佢仲想抵賴？真係吟詩吟唔甩啦。
English: The evidence is so clear, and he still wants to deny it? He really can't wriggle out of it.

17. 佈道大會

廣東話：教會下個禮拜會舉行佈道大會，歡迎大家參加。
English: The church will hold an evangelistic meeting next week; everyone is welcome to attend.

18. 寫手

廣東話：佢係一個好有才華嘅寫手，寫嘅文章好多人睇。
English: He is a very talented writer; many people read his articles.

19. 寫手

廣東話：呢本小說其實係請咗寫手代筆嘅，唔係作者本人寫。
English: This novel was actually ghostwritten by a hired writer; it wasn't written by the author himself.

20. 代打

廣東話：佢今日唔舒服，所以搵咗個朋友代打。
English: He's not feeling well today, so he found a friend to play on his behalf.

21. 茶碗

廣東話：日本茶道用嘅茶碗好講究，每一隻都有佢嘅特色。
English: The tea bowls used in Japanese tea ceremony are very particular; each one has its own characteristics.

22. 茶隔

廣東話：沖茶嘅時候用茶隔，就可以將茶葉同茶湯分開，唔使擔心飲到茶葉。
English: Using a tea strainer when brewing tea can separate the tea leaves from the tea, so you don't have to worry about drinking the leaves.

23. 只許州官放火，不准百姓點燈

廣東話：佢自己可以遲到早退，但係就要求下屬準時返工，真係只許州官放火，不准百姓點燈。
English: He can be late and leave early himself, but demands his subordinates be punctual; it's really "only the magistrate may set fires, while commoners may not light lamps."

24. 獨唱

廣東話：今晚嘅表演有佢一個人獨唱，好期待。
English: Tonight's performance features a solo by him; I'm really looking forward to it.

25. 快人快事

廣東話：佢係一個快人快事嘅人，答應咗嘅嘢一定會盡快做完。
English: He is a straightforward and efficient person; once he agrees to something, he will finish it as soon as possible.

26. 四腳獸

廣東話：公廁入面發現有四腳獸，保安即刻報警處理。
English: A "four-legged beast" was found in the public toilet, and security immediately called the police.

27. 無米粥

廣東話：呢單生意而家只係煲緊無米粥，大家唔好期望太高。
English: This deal is still just preliminary talks; everyone shouldn't have too high expectations.

28. 義會

廣東話：以前啲低下階層冇錢向銀行借，就會參加義會，集資應急。
English: In the past, lower-class people who couldn't borrow from banks would join mutual aid associations to pool funds for emergencies.

29. 榜文

廣東話：古代嘅榜文貼喺城門口，通知百姓最新嘅政令。
English: In ancient times, official notices were posted at the city gate to inform the public of the latest government decrees.

30. MK名

廣東話：佢個網名係「堅系醉愛絕對唯愛」，一睇就知係典型嘅 MK名。
English: His online name is "堅系醉愛絕對唯愛"; you can tell at a glance it's a typical MK name. [end of text]


